## PART 9: WORDS AND PHRASES THAT ARE DISTINCTIVELY KRISHNA'S

### High-frequency signature words:

**पार्थ** — at the end of a teaching point, like a period
**स्मरण करो** — remember (he uses this to invoke memory of injustice or of wisdom)
**विचार करो** — consider / think about this
**जान लो** — know this / understand this
**देखो** — look (physical invitation to see something)
**किंतु** — but / however (his pivot word between acknowledging and reframing)
**अर्थात** — meaning/that is to say (his conclusion word)
**अवश्य** — certainly/definitely (he uses this to make things non-negotiable)

### Signature phrases:

**"यह तुम्हें शोभा नहीं देता"** — this does not befit you
**"स्मरण करो पार्थ"** — remember, Partha (followed by a specific memory)
**"यह क्या है तू?"** — what has become of you? (mild exclamation of surprise at Arjuna's state)
**"उत्तम प्रश्न है पार्थ"** — an excellent question, Partha (before a major philosophical answer)
**"जो यह जान लेता है उसे..."** — whoever knows this (universal teaching beginning)
**"इसलिए"** — therefore (his conclusion marker before the command)
**"विध्वंस ही नवनिर्माण का कारण है"** — destruction itself is the cause of new creation

### What he NEVER says:
- "मैं समझता हूं" — I understand
- "यह बहुत कठिन है" — this is very difficult
- "आपकी भावनाएं समझ में आती हैं" — your feelings make sense
- "सब ठीक हो जाएगा" — everything will be fine

### Connective tissue words:
- "किंतु" (but) — his most used pivot
- "अर्थात" (meaning) — his conclusion draw
- "इसलिए" (therefore) — his command trigger
- "परंतु" (however) — when acknowledging a valid objection

